{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/516015-x-k-post-numbers-special-ranks","id":516015,"title":"X'k post numbers - Special Ranks?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-16T04:34:13-07:00","id":516015,"title":"X'k post numbers - Special Ranks?","content":"This is my, literally, 2000th post on the forum - so I want to congregat everyone for letting me in disussion for so long. I know I can be a very problematic co-disputant sometimes. Happy X-kilos for everyone writing this much stuff on Onyx Paths forums! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But to the idea - on other forums I saw there is Special Rank system. That users with posts numbers in thousends get to choose they own Title ( or are awarded one ) tha is shown under they user name. I suspect that this Forum engine also has possibility of this kind feature. So maybe Administration would think about it?<br /> <br /> I would probably want to be called &quot;Hamster Lord&quot;. ( Yeah, it's a joke with this name. ) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T06:33:22-07:00","id":516123,"title":"","content":"There used to be such a system in place. It was disabled. I forget why, but I remember a discussion about it in the Trouble Tickets forum a discussion which has since been deleted) in which I supported disabling it because I thought granting titles could be perceived as official favoritism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T07:00:16-07:00","id":516143,"title":"","content":"I've always felt like tying perks to post count, no matter how silly and trivial, projects value onto something that has no value and shouldn't have value. The number itself can be useful for a little contextual information now and then, but I've never liked the idea that people who post more often or have posted longer get pointed out by some status.<br /> <br /> Custom titles, though, I'd be entirely cool with. I'd just permit any user to set one rather than tying it to anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T07:01:22-07:00","id":516145,"title":"","content":"It was Leaper mokingly complaining about it + not being any reasons to have one.<br /> <br /> EDIT: for reference, after your first 1K you got the Senior Member title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T10:01:08-07:00","id":516261,"title":"","content":"I'm actually a fan of the titles thing, but the implementation is always wonky-there's no good way to give them out without touching on arbitrariness or favoritism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T15:12:47-07:00","id":524788,"title":"","content":"No special titles, they create issues within the community particularly when post count is seen as seniority, therefore adding nonexistent weight to whatever the person in question is posting. We don't want to reinforce any kind of notion of the site favoring someone due to the amount they post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Pos